# * balance report links with --base-url

# ** 1. Column headings link to the register for the column's period, as a
# period expression that reads back as the same span: a week is written
# out with its exclusive end date, not as an ISO week name.
<
2025-01-15 a
  assets:cash  10
  income

2025-01-22 b
  assets:cash  20
  income

$ hledger -f- bal -W -O html --base-url ''
> /<a href="register\?q=date:2025-01-13\.\.2025-01-20" title="[^"]*">2025-W03</
>= 0

# ** 2. The heading keeps its display form; only the link's term changes.
<
2025-01-15 a
  assets:cash  10
  income

2025-02-20 b
  assets:cash  20
  income

$ hledger -f- bal -M --period-titles=dates -O html --base-url ''
> /<a href="register\?q=date:2025-01" title="[^"]*">2025-01-01\.\.2025-01-31</
>= 0

# ** 3. A span that is not a calendar period keeps its last day: the
# heading shows the inclusive end date, the term the exclusive one.
<
2025-01-15 a
  assets:cash  10
  income

2025-02-20 b
  assets:cash  20
  income

$ hledger -f- bal -M -p 2025-01-15..2025-03-01 -O html --base-url ''
> /<a href="register\?q=date:2025-01-15\.\.2025-02-15" title="[^"]*">2025-01-15\.\.2025-02-14</
>= 0

# ** 4. The same term in the tidy layout's period column.
<
2025-01-15 a
  assets:cash  10
  income

$ hledger -f- bal -W --layout=tidy -O html --base-url ''
> /<a href="register\?q=inacct:assets:cash\+date:2025-01-13\.\.2025-01-20" title="[^"]*">2025-W03</
>= 0

# ** 5. An inacct: term in the query is not carried into the links, which
# name their own account.
<
2025-01-15 a
  assets:cash  10
  income

$ hledger -f- bal -O html --base-url '' inacct:assets
> /<a href="register\?q=inacct:assets:cash" title="[^"]*">assets:cash</
>= 0

# ** 6. Without --base-url, no links.
<
2025-01-15 a
  assets:cash  10
  income

$ hledger -f- bal -W -O html
> !/<a href/
>= 0

# ** 7. Each figure links to the register that derives it: the account's
# transactions in the column's period.
<
2025-01-10 salary
  assets:bank:checking  100
  income:salary

2025-01-20 fee
  assets:bank  -5
  expenses:fees

2025-02-15 lunch
  expenses:food  10
  assets:bank:checking

$ hledger -f- bal -M -O html --base-url ''
> /<a href="register\?q=inacct:assets:bank:checking\+date:2025-02" title="Show the transactions that make up this amount">/
>= 0

# ** 8. A list-mode parent whose subaccount has its own row shows its own
# postings only, and links with inacctonly:.
<
2025-01-10 salary
  assets:bank:checking  100
  income:salary

2025-01-20 fee
  assets:bank  -5
  expenses:fees

2025-02-15 lunch
  expenses:food  10
  assets:bank:checking

$ hledger -f- bal -M -O html --base-url ''
> /<a href="register\?q=inacctonly:assets:bank" title="Show transactions affecting this account but not subaccounts">assets:bank</
>= 0

# ** 9. Its figures likewise.
<
2025-01-10 salary
  assets:bank:checking  100
  income:salary

2025-01-20 fee
  assets:bank  -5
  expenses:fees

2025-02-15 lunch
  expenses:food  10
  assets:bank:checking

$ hledger -f- bal -M -O html --base-url ''
> /<a href="register\?q=inacctonly:assets:bank\+date:2025-01" title="Show the transactions that make up this amount">/
>= 0

# ** 10. A figure that looks zero has an empty register, and no link.
<
2025-01-10 salary
  assets:bank:checking  100
  income:salary

2025-01-20 fee
  assets:bank  -5
  expenses:fees

2025-02-15 lunch
  expenses:food  10
  assets:bank:checking

$ hledger -f- bal -M -O html --base-url ''
> !/inacctonly:assets:bank\+date:2025-02/
>= 0

# ** 11. The totals row links each column's total to the register of
# everything in the report's query for that period.
<
2025-01-20 fee
  assets:bank  -5
  expenses:fees

2025-02-15 lunch
  expenses:food  10
  assets:bank

$ hledger -f- bal -M -O html --base-url '' expenses
> /<a href="register\?q=date:2025-02\+expenses" title="Show the transactions that make up this total">/
>= 0

# ** 12. A row total links to the whole report span. (An average has no
# register, so no link.)
<
2025-01-20 fee
  assets:bank  -5
  expenses:fees

2025-02-15 lunch
  expenses:food  10
  assets:bank

$ hledger -f- bal -M -T -A -O html --base-url ''
> /<a href="register\?q=inacct:assets:bank\+date:2025-01-01\.\.2025-03-01" title="Show the transactions that make up this amount">/
>= 0

# ** 12b. The average has none.
<
2025-01-20 fee
  assets:bank  -5
  expenses:fees

2025-02-15 lunch
  expenses:food  10
  assets:bank

$ hledger -f- bal -M -T -A -O html --base-url ''
> !/class="amount rowaverage"><a /
>= 0

# ** 13. With historical balances, the links ask the register for its
# historical mode, so that its running balance ends on the figure.
<
2025-01-20 fee
  assets:bank  -5
  expenses:fees

2025-02-15 lunch
  expenses:food  10
  assets:bank

$ hledger -f- bal -M -H -O html --base-url ''
> /<a href="register\?q=inacct:assets:bank\+date:2025-02&amp;accum=historical" title="Show the transactions behind this balance">/
>= 0

# ** 14. The account name's link too.
<
2025-01-20 fee
  assets:bank  -5
  expenses:fees

2025-02-15 lunch
  expenses:food  10
  assets:bank

$ hledger -f- bal -M -H -O html --base-url ''
> /<a href="register\?q=inacct:assets:bank&amp;accum=historical" title="Show transactions affecting this account and subaccounts">assets:bank</
>= 0

# ** 15. A cumulative figure's register runs from the report's start.
<
2025-01-20 fee
  assets:bank  -5
  expenses:fees

2025-02-15 lunch
  expenses:food  10
  assets:bank

$ hledger -f- bal -M --cumulative -O html --base-url ''
> /<a href="register\?q=inacct:assets:bank\+date:2025-01-01\.\.2025-03-01" title="Show the transactions that make up this amount">/
>= 0

# ** 15b. The first column's figure links to the first period alone.
<
2025-01-20 fee
  assets:bank  -5
  expenses:fees

2025-02-15 lunch
  assets:bank  -10
  expenses:food

$ hledger -f- bal -M --cumulative -O html --base-url ''
> /<a href="register\?q=inacct:assets:bank\+date:2025-01" title="Show the transactions that make up this amount">/
>= 0

# ** 16. Figures that are not sums of postings do not link.
<
2025-01-20 fee
  assets:bank  -5
  expenses:fees

$ hledger -f- bal -M --count -O html --base-url ''
> !/<a href="register\?q=inacct:assets:bank\+date:/
>= 0

# ** 17. Account names still do.
<
2025-01-20 fee
  assets:bank  -5
  expenses:fees

$ hledger -f- bal -M --count -O html --base-url ''
> /<a href="register\?q=inacct:assets:bank" title="[^"]*">assets:bank</
>= 0

# ** 18. A depth-clipped row sums its subaccounts, and links with inacct:.
<
2025-01-20 fee
  assets:bank:checking  -5
  expenses:fees

$ hledger -f- bal depth:1 -O html --base-url ''
> /<a href="register\?q=inacct:assets\+depth:1" title="Show transactions affecting this account and subaccounts">assets</
>= 0

# ** 19. In a single-period report the figures link to the account's
# register for the report period.
<
2025-01-20 fee
  assets:bank  -5
  expenses:fees

2025-02-15 lunch
  expenses:food  10
  assets:bank

$ hledger -f- bal -p 2025-01 -O html --base-url '' expenses
> /<a href="register\?q=inacct:expenses:fees\+date:2025-01\+expenses" title="Show the transactions that make up this amount">/
>= 0

# ** 20. And the total to everything's.
<
2025-01-20 fee
  assets:bank  -5
  expenses:fees

2025-02-15 lunch
  expenses:food  10
  assets:bank

$ hledger -f- bal -p 2025-01 -O html --base-url '' expenses
> /<a href="register\?q=date:2025-01\+expenses" title="Show the transactions that make up this total">/
>= 0

# ** 21. FODS output carries the same links.
<
2025-01-20 fee
  assets:bank  -5
  expenses:fees

$ hledger -f- bal -M -O fods --base-url ''
> /<text:a xlink:href='register\?q=inacct:assets:bank\+date:2025-01'>/
>= 0

# ** 22. A report using secondary dates asks the register to use them too.
<
2025-01-31=2025-02-02 late fee
  assets:bank  -7
  expenses:fees

2025-02-15 lunch
  expenses:food  10
  assets:bank

$ hledger -f- bal -M --date2 -O html --base-url ''
> /<a href="register\?q=inacct:assets:bank\+date2:2025-02" title="Show the transactions that make up this amount">/
>= 0
